1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,870
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,380
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:10,250
- Mom.
- Honey, you're here? Yes.

4
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:13,120
Hello, sir.

5
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:16,590
- What brings you here?
- Where is my mother?

6
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:18,160
Where is she, Dr. Ju? What?

7
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:20,530
What is wrong with her,
and how bad is it?

8
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:22,160
If you mean your mother...

9
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:25,660
Are you talking about Mrs. Choi
from the chicken restaurant?

10
00:00:25,730 --> 00:00:29,970
Yes, yes. She is my mother.
Where is my mother?

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,340
- She is alive, right?
- Of course. It is not serious,

12
00:00:33,370 --> 00:00:36,780
so do not worry.
She is resting well inside.

13
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:40,980
By the way, if she is your mother,

14
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:43,850
what is your relationship
with Ms. Jo?

15
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,050
Well...

16
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:49,890
- You see, the thing is...
- Honey.

17
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,320
You should hurry inside
to see Mother.

18
00:00:52,390 --> 00:00:53,960
That is not what matters right now.

19
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:56,260
You should be out making money.

20
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:59,030
Why did you come running
all the way here?

21
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:02,700
Mother, what on earth happened?

22
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,770
How did this happen?

23
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:09,310
I just ate a little something,
and it gave me severe indigestion.

24
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:13,780
- Why are you here, anyway?
- What do you mean, why?

25
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:16,310
My wife called me,
so I rushed right over.

26
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:18,920
What did you eat, Mom?

27
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:21,820
Ma'am, so this gentleman
is your son.

28
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:23,720
Yes.

29
00:01:24,290 --> 00:01:27,930
Yes, Dr. Ju, I gave birth to him.

30
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,660
Your IV is almost finished,

31
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:34,270
but you need to head back inside
and let it run out before you leave.

32
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:36,500
All right.

33
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:39,600
Mom, go on inside. Let me help you.

34
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:44,040
Easy, take it slow. Easy.
Careful, careful.

35
00:01:44,910 --> 00:01:49,150
Take it slow, take it slow.
All right, have a seat first. Yes.

36
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,980
I told you, it is just indigestion.

37
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:55,090
Yes. Right.

38
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:58,790
Color 194052. Classic Blue.

39
00:01:59,390 --> 00:02:04,030
Okay, 173938. Very Peri.

40
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:09,100
Okay, 181750. Viva...

41
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:10,540
Viva what?

42
00:02:11,470 --> 00:02:12,540
Magenta.

43
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:16,210
Got them all right.
Good job, Kkangda.

44
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:20,580
Ms. Kang Da Mi.

45
00:02:21,410 --> 00:02:22,410
Yes, Head Designer Cha.

46
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,820
Is there something else
you need me to do?

47
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:28,750
Do you always talk to yourself
out loud like that?

48
00:02:29,590 --> 00:02:32,760
No. I was just memorizing
the fabric sample names...

49
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:35,460
- and their numbers in my head.
- Give me a break...

50
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:37,930
Code 1750. Viva Magenta.

51
00:02:38,630 --> 00:02:42,500
That is what I was just memorizing.
How did you know?

52
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:47,140
And your nickname is Kkangda, right?
I heard you, so of course I know.

53
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:49,470
It is not like I have
some mind-reading ability.

54
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:53,010
I am sorry.

55
00:02:54,050 --> 00:02:57,480
The truth is, I tend to talk
to myself a bit.

56
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,280
Head Designer Cha,

57
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,690
almost everyone who has worked
in retail customer service...

58
00:03:01,950 --> 00:03:04,820
has this kind of habit.

59
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:08,460
So it is an occupational hazard,
is that it?

60
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:10,460
I suppose so.

61
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:11,760
Well, fair enough.

62
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:14,730
Most jobs are tough to endure.

63
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,830
That is how it is.

64
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:18,370
Then again, enduring it
is also how you succeed.

65
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:26,610
Head Designer Cha, while I have you,
may I ask you something?

66
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:30,950
The sample box assigned to me...

67
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:33,050
went missing on evaluation day.

68
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:36,790
Assistant Manager Kang
from Product Planning...

69
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:38,090
found and returned it safely,

70
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:41,160
so the evaluation went smoothly.
What about it?

71
00:03:42,990 --> 00:03:44,860
Well, no matter how much
I think about it, it is strange.

72
00:03:45,130 --> 00:03:48,130
I searched high and low
everywhere for it.

73
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:49,700
It definitely was not there.

74
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,440
Kang Da Mi,

75
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:56,840
are you aware
that you can be a bit clumsy?

76
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:00,450
Sometimes, yes.

77
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:03,950
Whenever a problem arises,

78
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:06,120
you insist you can manage it...

79
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:08,550
all alone, from start to finish.

80
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:09,990
You overestimate your ability
and act on your own.

81
00:04:10,090 --> 00:04:12,260
Are you aware of that too?

82
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:16,230
I am truly sorry
for reporting it late.

83
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,560
However...

84
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,300
However?

85
00:04:20,330 --> 00:04:21,970
What could possibly follow
that "however"?

86
00:04:22,230 --> 00:04:24,700
Even when I worked
at the department store,

87
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,770
double-checking was always
standard for me.

88
00:04:28,270 --> 00:04:29,940
If even one digit
in the inventory...

89
00:04:30,010 --> 00:04:31,010
or cash register
totals did not match,

90
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,310
I had to find the cause
and fix it...

91
00:04:32,410 --> 00:04:33,540
before I could leave work.

92
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:36,310
Being an assistant in fashion
is new to me, sure,

93
00:04:36,410 --> 00:04:38,520
but just receiving an item
from a courier...

94
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:40,720
is something I would
never mess up on.

95
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:42,120
That is what I am saying.

96
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:46,520
So are you going to
keep obsessing over this?

97
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:50,190
- Pardon?
- I mean,

98
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,400
are you going to let this
keep bothering you?

99
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:54,100
Will it get in the way
of your future work?

100
00:04:54,170 --> 00:04:55,170
That is what I am asking.

101
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,470
Honestly speaking, yes.

102
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:01,970
Still, the evaluation ended well,

103
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:05,680
- so my unease is just...
- All right, enough. That is fine.

104
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:09,710
You do your job, Kang Da Mi,
and I will do mine.

105
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:10,880
Back to work.

106
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:12,950
Yes.

107
00:05:22,890 --> 00:05:24,860
Mom, be careful. Careful.

108
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:29,230
Wait, Mom. Honey, hold this.

109
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,370
Mom, let me carry you
on my back, okay?

110
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:33,400
Mom,
you don't have any energy right now.

111
00:05:33,570 --> 00:05:34,670
Come on, hurry.

112
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:37,280
Please do, Mother.
You can't walk like this.

113
00:05:37,410 --> 00:05:38,540
Get off me, you brat.

114
00:05:38,610 --> 00:05:40,650
I would rather die
than be indebted to you.

115
00:05:40,810 --> 00:05:42,910
- Oh, my. Look at her.
- Mother.

116
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:45,550
Mom, just trust me.
I will support you.

117
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:49,050
Honey, what are you doing?
Hurry and help support her.

118
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,760
- Oh, right. Don't worry, Mother.
- Hurry, that's right.

119
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:53,460
- I'm here, too.
- That's it, that's it.

120
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,660
Let go of me, you two.

121
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:58,560
I can walk to my own house
by myself.

122
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:03,200
- What if someone sees us?
- Mother. Honey.

123
00:06:03,270 --> 00:06:04,900
Where are we going, anyway?

124
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:07,740
Where do you think?
We should go to our house.

125
00:06:08,110 --> 00:06:09,740
- Here, Mom.
- Right, our place, our place.

126
00:06:09,810 --> 00:06:10,810
Let's go quickly.

127
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:13,180
- Let go of me.
- Mom.

128
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,380
- Mother.
- Take it easy, Mom. Slowly.

129
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:17,220
- Mother, careful. Careful.
- Careful, careful. Be careful.

130
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:19,880
It's the area
on the inside of the lobby...

131
00:06:20,050 --> 00:06:21,320
where packages are placed.

132
00:06:22,150 --> 00:06:24,660
The evaluation sample went missing
and was found again,

133
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:27,290
so I'd like to check
who came and went around there.

134
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,900
I'm sorry, Head Designer Cha.

135
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:32,530
The camera there
has been acting up...

136
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:34,270
for a few days,
so it's being serviced.

137
00:06:34,430 --> 00:06:35,570
Really?

138
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:37,640
So you're saying we can't check it?

139
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,040
Yes, sir.

140
00:06:40,910 --> 00:06:42,870
In that case...

141
00:06:56,190 --> 00:06:58,620
Ms. Jo Mi Mi, you will go in
for testing early tomorrow morning.

142
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,260
You can sleep here tonight.

143
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:03,230
Does it usually happen this quickly?

144
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:05,160
I thought I'd just hear
the explanation and go.

145
00:07:05,230 --> 00:07:08,700
Dr. Ju Kyung Ho called us.

146
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,200
He asked us to take care of you
so you can get the tests you need.

147
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:13,670
You have an endoscopy...

148
00:07:13,770 --> 00:07:14,870
and an ultrasound
scheduled tomorrow,

149
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:17,280
so you must fast starting tonight,
including water.

150
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:19,610
Why do I need another endoscopy?

151
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:22,710
It's an ultrasound test to examine
the inside in more detail.

152
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:24,250
Are you currently
taking any medications?

153
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:28,390
- No.
- Please read this over and sign...

154
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:29,650
the consent form on the last page.

155
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,120
Okay.

156
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,430
Dr. Ju, what brings you...

157
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,970
I will be back in a little while.

158
00:07:43,430 --> 00:07:44,470
All right.

159
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:49,210
I stopped by
to see how you were doing.

160
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:52,380
May I sit down for a moment?

161
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:55,810
Of course, Dr. Ju.

162
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:06,990
Welcome, Head Designer Cha.

163
00:08:07,790 --> 00:08:09,960
- What brings you here?
- Hello.

164
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:13,930
Regarding the sample box
that Kang Da Mi lost earlier...

165
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:17,000
I just went to the security office
to check the CCTV.

166
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:19,540
Excuse me? The CCTV?

167
00:08:24,810 --> 00:08:26,310
Yes, the CCTV.

168
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,680
Assistant Manager Kang,
could you tell me again...

169
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:31,020
where you found that sample box?

170
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,660
You remember the exact spot, right?

171
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,090
I found it behind the lobby,

172
00:08:40,790 --> 00:08:42,230
tucked between some other boxes.

173
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:44,930
I was in such a rush
to bring it over...

174
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,160
that I do not remember much else.

175
00:08:46,530 --> 00:08:47,530
Head Designer Cha.

176
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:52,970
Are you interrogating
my team member right now?

177
00:08:53,770 --> 00:08:56,170
No, I just wanted to make sure...

178
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:58,940
where exactly
she found that sample box.

179
00:08:59,410 --> 00:09:01,650
I asked security about it
this morning,

180
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:03,650
and since the cameras were down,
I couldn't check.

181
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:04,680
But either way,

182
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:08,020
Assistant Manager Kang
recovered the lost samples,

183
00:09:08,190 --> 00:09:09,890
and the evaluation went well,
did it not?

184
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:13,460
Treating someone
who helped out like this is a bit...

185
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,990
- I do not think this is right.
- Look, I am sorry.

186
00:09:17,230 --> 00:09:19,060
If I offended you, I am truly sorry,
Assistant Manager Kang.

187
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:20,830
No matter how much
I thought about it,

188
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:23,170
it just did not seem like a mistake
Kang Da Mi would make,

189
00:09:23,230 --> 00:09:24,400
so I guess it came out
the wrong way.

190
00:09:24,470 --> 00:09:26,470
I apologize. Thank you.

191
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:33,140
Team Leader Cha.

192
00:09:33,910 --> 00:09:36,010
You just took my side, did you not?

193
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,980
Well, I am your team leader.

194
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,890
Let us head out together,
Team Leader Cha.

195
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:52,360
Mother. I made it mild on purpose.

196
00:09:53,030 --> 00:09:55,900
Even if you do not have an appetite,
try to eat slowly.

197
00:09:56,370 --> 00:09:59,740
- I said I am fine.
- Careful, it is hot.

198
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:04,410
Mom, let me blow on it for you.
Just a second.

199
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:11,750
Did your nose bridge collapse?

200
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,990
I was worried about that too,

201
00:10:15,290 --> 00:10:18,320
but it is fine
other than a slight throbbing.

202
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:21,490
It is not fine.

203
00:10:21,990 --> 00:10:24,330
Mother, he was groaning
about his nose hurting...

204
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:26,060
all night in his sleep.

205
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,970
It broke my heart so much.

206
00:10:29,470 --> 00:10:33,070
What is done is done,

207
00:10:34,470 --> 00:10:36,670
but I am more worried
about what comes next.

208
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:44,720
- You are early.
- Seung Yun!

209
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:46,480
Can we talk for a second?

210
00:10:51,790 --> 00:10:52,790
What is it?

211
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:55,030
About earlier in front of
Assistant Manager Kang.

212
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:58,260
I am sorry if I upset you.

213
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:01,000
What do you have
to be sorry for, man?

214
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,830
She is on your team,
so what you said was natural.

215
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:04,240
Do Yun, I didn't know...

216
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:06,340
you'd gone to check the CCTV.

217
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,170
That was something
I should have done.

218
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:11,580
Hearing that Da Mi made
that kind of mistake bothered me,

219
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:14,410
and it felt odd,
so I went to look into it myself.

220
00:11:15,310 --> 00:11:17,680
Too bad nothing was recorded.

221
00:11:18,450 --> 00:11:20,790
That is why I went to ask
Assistant Manager Kang directly...

222
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:22,490
since she came to see me.

223
00:11:22,650 --> 00:11:26,290
Hey, Do Yun, are you usually
this interested in every employee?

224
00:11:28,230 --> 00:11:29,330
Are you talking about Kang Da Mi?

225
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:31,960
No, just saying.

226
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,300
She's not even on your team,

227
00:11:34,370 --> 00:11:36,130
yet you went all the way
to security,

228
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,200
so I was just curious.

229
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,100
Want me to be honest?

230
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:41,810
Yes.

231
00:11:42,670 --> 00:11:43,670
To be honest...

232
00:11:45,610 --> 00:11:47,010
I like Kang Da Mi, Seung Yun.

233
00:11:49,010 --> 00:11:51,220
- Really?
- Yes.

234
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:52,950
She's a good person.

235
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:54,820
So please help her out.

236
00:11:55,690 --> 00:11:56,690
It's her first time as an assistant,

237
00:11:56,750 --> 00:12:00,190
so there's a lot she doesn't know,
but she's definitely not a slacker.

238
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:01,660
Okay.

239
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:04,730
I'll keep that in mind.

240
00:12:05,630 --> 00:12:06,630
Still, unlike you,

241
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:09,270
I don't openly help people
or give them special treatment.

242
00:12:10,430 --> 00:12:11,440
What do you mean?

243
00:12:11,570 --> 00:12:14,210
I'll teach her the job properly,
my own way.

244
00:12:14,710 --> 00:12:15,710
That's what I mean.

245
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:25,820
Was it a mistake to tell him?

246
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:32,460
- Mom, today our Team Leader Cha...
- You're home, sweetheart?

247
00:12:33,190 --> 00:12:34,630
Ye Ri.

248
00:12:35,890 --> 00:12:39,960
- Wait, why is our landlady here?
- Well, you see...

249
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:42,570
Ye Ri, say hello first, okay?

250
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:44,570
Hello.

251
00:12:45,270 --> 00:12:46,270
Dad.

252
00:12:47,470 --> 00:12:50,840
She wasn't feeling well at all,

253
00:12:50,910 --> 00:12:52,540
so your mom and I brought her here.

254
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:55,050
Your mom made her some porridge too.

255
00:12:55,110 --> 00:12:59,320
Even if she's our landlady,
why do we have to nurse her?

256
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,620
Do all tenants do this?

257
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:06,020
- I should get going.
- Where could you go in this state,

258
00:13:06,090 --> 00:13:07,220
Mom?

259
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:09,990
- "Mom"?
- Yes.

260
00:13:10,490 --> 00:13:13,600
That's right. She's my mom.

261
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:15,600
She's not just our landlady.

262
00:13:16,370 --> 00:13:19,300
Now greet your paternal grandmother.

263
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:20,700
What?

264
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:24,070
I thought you said
she died years ago.

265
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:26,810
- Both of you told me that.
- Ye Ri.

266
00:13:27,810 --> 00:13:31,020
I'll explain everything later.
Just greet your grandmother fir...

267
00:13:31,650 --> 00:13:34,490
Actually, give her a deep bow, okay?

268
00:13:35,090 --> 00:13:38,460
You shouldn't bow deeply
to sick people.

269
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:40,220
Ye Ri?

270
00:13:40,690 --> 00:13:43,860
- Sweetheart, come here.
- Go on.

271
00:13:43,930 --> 00:13:46,230
- Yes, hurry, Ye Ri.
- Yes, go on.

272
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,750
The spitting image.

273
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:10,890
Well, the apple doesn't fall
far from the tree.

274
00:14:11,890 --> 00:14:14,330
Right? She looks just like me,
doesn't she, Mom?

275
00:14:16,490 --> 00:14:17,760
No, your father.

276
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,000
These long fingers...

277
00:14:21,930 --> 00:14:24,570
and this flat thumb.

278
00:14:25,270 --> 00:14:27,270
Mother, our daughter...

279
00:14:27,770 --> 00:14:29,470
works at a really great company.

280
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:31,510
It's a fashion company
called Hwanggeum Apparel.

281
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:34,850
- She's an assistant manager there.
- Let me see.

282
00:14:36,610 --> 00:14:39,120
This is our first time meeting
as grandmother and granddaughter,

283
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:41,890
and I came empty-handed.

284
00:14:47,730 --> 00:14:48,790
Why is it only 300 dollars?

285
00:14:49,330 --> 00:14:50,490
You should make it 600 dollars.

286
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:52,430
Grandma.

287
00:14:53,230 --> 00:14:56,670
I barely earned even this much
to give you.

288
00:14:57,740 --> 00:15:00,840
I'll pay the remaining
300 dollars next month, I promise.

289
00:15:01,810 --> 00:15:03,740
I'll let it slide
just this one month.

290
00:15:03,810 --> 00:15:05,110
If you don't pay the rest
next month,

291
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:06,310
I'll kick you out right away,

292
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:08,610
- so consider yourself warned.
- Yes.

293
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:10,810
Thank you, yes.

294
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:22,260
This is all I have on me.

295
00:15:22,930 --> 00:15:24,430
Buy yourself something delicious.

296
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:26,360
Pardon?

297
00:15:27,770 --> 00:15:30,870
Yes, thank you, Grandma.

298
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:33,600
Mother.

299
00:15:33,670 --> 00:15:36,610
Please stay and spend tonight
here with us.

300
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:39,380
You can catch up on this and that
with Ye Ri too, right?

301
00:15:40,610 --> 00:15:41,950
What?

302
00:15:44,210 --> 00:15:45,420
Please do, Grandma.

303
00:15:45,950 --> 00:15:47,320
Ever since I was little,

304
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:49,320
I've envied friends
who had a grandma.

305
00:15:56,590 --> 00:15:59,160
(My Mi Mi)

306
00:16:01,930 --> 00:16:03,370
She's still not answering.

307
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,240
Is she sleeping?

308
00:16:11,310 --> 00:16:12,840
I told you to go home.

309
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:15,680
What are the flowers for?

310
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:22,650
This hospital room will feel bleak
if you stay alone until tomorrow.

311
00:16:22,650 --> 00:16:23,720
Isn't this much better?

312
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:28,160
They're my favorite. Sunflowers.

313
00:16:29,230 --> 00:16:30,430
They're really pretty.

314
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,030
By the way, Dr. Ju.

315
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:40,040
Just how serious is it?

316
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:43,070
I got a call...

317
00:16:43,410 --> 00:16:44,910
telling me to come right away,
and then...

318
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:46,010
you tell me to get admitted.

319
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:48,280
If it were nothing,

320
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:50,250
you wouldn't be doing this.

321
00:16:52,150 --> 00:16:54,490
There's no need to worry beforehand.

322
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:57,760
We won't know for sure until
the exact test results come out.

323
00:16:58,160 --> 00:17:00,490
Even if something concerning
comes up,

324
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:02,630
you can just get treated
and recover.

325
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,800
That's why doctors like me are here.

326
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,930
Yes, thank you, Dr. Ju.

327
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,300
I'll go see the doctor in charge.

328
00:17:15,010 --> 00:17:17,440
If you're in pain,

329
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:19,110
don't just endure it...

330
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:22,680
Please call for help.

331
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:25,320
Okay.

332
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:54,080
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

333
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:55,180
Hey.

334
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:56,980
You again?

335
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:59,120
I asked you to do a little work,

336
00:17:59,180 --> 00:18:01,690
so how many clay pots
have you broken already?

337
00:18:02,290 --> 00:18:03,820
Are you the king of destruction?

338
00:18:03,820 --> 00:18:06,090
Are you determined
to ruin this business?

339
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:09,130
Auntie, did I do it on purpose?

340
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,260
Don't you appreciate the kindness
of someone helping?

341
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:15,770
Who's helping whom?
This is your mom's restaurant.

342
00:18:15,830 --> 00:18:17,700
You ought to be doing this anyway.

343
00:18:21,370 --> 00:18:23,370
I can't go home,
but I should at least...

344
00:18:23,810 --> 00:18:25,480
tell them that I'm at the hospital.

345
00:18:35,290 --> 00:18:37,520
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

346
00:18:37,590 --> 00:18:39,920
Mi Mi, where on earth are you?

347
00:18:41,430 --> 00:18:45,260
- Is that Mom?
- Ri Ja, I...

348
00:18:47,230 --> 00:18:48,900
The thing is, right now,
I'm at the hospital...

349
00:18:48,970 --> 00:18:50,670
I'm working myself to death here.

350
00:18:51,070 --> 00:18:53,570
Mrs. Choi isn't here,
and neither are you.

351
00:18:53,770 --> 00:18:56,310
Do you want to see
your only sister collapse?

352
00:18:57,370 --> 00:18:59,510
- I'm sorry.
- Did you go out...

353
00:18:59,580 --> 00:19:02,110
wearing that yellow dress again?

354
00:19:02,110 --> 00:19:03,650
Did you really run off
with some guy...

355
00:19:03,710 --> 00:19:07,520
and go gallivanting around?
Are you having an affair?

356
00:19:09,990 --> 00:19:13,190
Why aren't you saying anything?
I asked if you're having an affair.

357
00:19:14,930 --> 00:19:16,530
Fine, yes, you're right.

358
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:19,000
What?

359
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:21,230
I'm having an affair, all right?

360
00:19:21,870 --> 00:19:23,800
I got so swept away
dancing with a man...

361
00:19:23,870 --> 00:19:25,200
that I completely
lost track of time.

362
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:26,600
Happy now?

363
00:19:27,170 --> 00:19:30,710
- Have you lost your mind?
- Why?

364
00:19:31,070 --> 00:19:34,010
Am I not allowed to do that?
Is it a crime for me to step away...

365
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:35,210
from the restaurant
for just one day?

366
00:19:37,110 --> 00:19:38,280
I won't be coming...

367
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:41,920
Actually, I'm not coming home.
Just so you know.

368
00:19:43,950 --> 00:19:46,560
Mi Mi? Hello?

369
00:19:46,620 --> 00:19:48,960
Mi Mi. Ms. Jo.

370
00:19:49,230 --> 00:19:50,290
My gosh.

371
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:54,870
What did Mom say? Where is she?

372
00:19:56,430 --> 00:19:57,500
Your mother says...

373
00:19:58,100 --> 00:20:00,500
- she's staying out tonight.
- What?

374
00:20:03,810 --> 00:20:08,510
My mom staying out overnight?
No way, give me a break.

375
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:11,650
Hey, what are you doing?

376
00:20:11,850 --> 00:20:15,150
- Clean the rest of this up.
- Auntie, something urgent...

377
00:20:15,220 --> 00:20:16,520
just came up,

378
00:20:16,690 --> 00:20:18,260
so I'll be back in a flash.
Right back.

379
00:20:18,590 --> 00:20:20,420
- Hey, Gang Nam.
- I'll be right back.

380
00:20:20,490 --> 00:20:21,490
Gang Nam.

381
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:28,730
I swear, this family is killing me.

382
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:53,320
Since I made 600 dollars,

383
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:57,960
I'll give you 300 dollars.

384
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:07,970
- Thank you for the ride home.
- Who's that punk?

385
00:21:09,770 --> 00:21:11,140
Have a good night, Director.

386
00:21:11,410 --> 00:21:13,210
You're sending me off
after coming this far?

387
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:15,210
Won't you even offer me
a cup of coffee?

388
00:21:15,510 --> 00:21:19,720
Even though I said I'd come alone,
I appreciate you driving me home.

389
00:21:19,850 --> 00:21:23,120
- However, Director...
- Go ahead, Mi Seon. Speak freely.

390
00:21:24,550 --> 00:21:27,760
Your family must be waiting for you.
You should head home.

391
00:21:28,030 --> 00:21:31,930
I told you, my wife took the kids
to visit her parents.

392
00:21:34,930 --> 00:21:35,970
I'll buy you coffee...

393
00:21:36,530 --> 00:21:40,770
at work tomorrow. Good night.

394
00:21:41,940 --> 00:21:45,710
All right, buy it tomorrow.
I'll have a vanilla latte.

395
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:51,280
A vanilla latte? How ridiculous.
What a jerk.

396
00:21:54,950 --> 00:21:56,020
Have you lost your mind?

397
00:21:56,490 --> 00:21:57,550
You scared me.

398
00:21:58,120 --> 00:21:59,320
What are you doing here?

399
00:21:59,460 --> 00:22:01,660
What are you doing?
You are a mother.

400
00:22:02,830 --> 00:22:04,290
Who is that sleazy jerk?

401
00:22:06,330 --> 00:22:08,030
He is the director at my clinic.

402
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:11,200
- He's my boss.
- I don't care if he's your boss.

403
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:14,740
Why is he trying to creep into
a single woman's house?

404
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:17,510
What kind of signals
were you sending...

405
00:22:17,570 --> 00:22:19,310
to have a guy like that
clinging to you already?

406
00:22:19,740 --> 00:22:22,150
Watch your mouth.
Who's sending signals?

407
00:22:22,510 --> 00:22:24,210
Did you see me do that? Did you?

408
00:22:28,250 --> 00:22:30,550
Here, 300 dollars.

409
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:33,760
Why should I take this?

410
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:36,030
If you want to give me money,
make it 30,000...

411
00:22:36,630 --> 00:22:40,730
No, make it 300,000 dollars.
I'll take that as damages.

412
00:22:44,430 --> 00:22:45,540
Hey, Mi Seon.

413
00:22:46,570 --> 00:22:48,640
Mi Seon, I'm sorry.

414
00:22:48,710 --> 00:22:50,640
I take back what I said
about sending signals.

415
00:22:51,070 --> 00:22:52,640
It just slipped out. I'm sorry.

416
00:22:53,540 --> 00:22:55,050
I'm sorry, Mi Seon.

417
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,160
Grandma.

418
00:23:14,660 --> 00:23:16,000
Back in the day,

419
00:23:16,570 --> 00:23:17,930
when people skipped out
on their debts,

420
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,600
you were really good
at tracking them down, right?

421
00:23:19,870 --> 00:23:23,110
- I was. Why?
- Just curious.

422
00:23:24,010 --> 00:23:27,880
If someone purposely disappears,
how do you even track them down?

423
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:31,310
Man, when Mother was younger,

424
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:33,120
she would go to
the ends of the earth...

425
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:34,920
to collect every last dime
owed to her.

426
00:23:36,220 --> 00:23:38,020
Nobody in this entire country...

427
00:23:38,090 --> 00:23:39,590
could hold a candle to Grandma
in that department.

428
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:42,860
Tell me your secret, Grandma.

429
00:23:43,430 --> 00:23:44,430
Please?

430
00:23:44,830 --> 00:23:47,660
If you start out thinking
you can't find someone,

431
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:52,800
you won't. Whether they
stole someone's money...

432
00:23:53,170 --> 00:23:55,910
or committed some other crime,

433
00:23:56,870 --> 00:23:58,140
in all my years of life,

434
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:00,910
I have learned...

435
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:04,710
that they always slip up eventually.

436
00:24:05,650 --> 00:24:08,290
As long as you don't give up first.

437
00:24:10,690 --> 00:24:11,990
Actually, Mother,

438
00:24:11,990 --> 00:24:14,390
there's something
I wanted to discuss with you.

439
00:24:14,930 --> 00:24:15,930
Yes?

440
00:24:16,560 --> 00:24:20,060
About having Se Na
collect that debt.

441
00:24:20,130 --> 00:24:23,030
I would like you to call it off.

442
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:26,100
Why, Mom?
I want to collect that money...

443
00:24:26,170 --> 00:24:28,140
and get Grandma's investment.

444
00:24:29,510 --> 00:24:31,710
I'll teach her a firm lesson...

445
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:34,210
so she won't waste money, Mother.

446
00:24:34,710 --> 00:24:36,980
I am sure Se Na has learned
her lesson by now.

447
00:24:37,580 --> 00:24:38,580
Right.

448
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:41,520
She is still young,
so she needs to study more, Mother.

449
00:24:42,020 --> 00:24:45,190
Jin Hee has already looked into
plans for her to study abroad.

450
00:24:47,190 --> 00:24:48,330
Jin Hee.

451
00:24:49,730 --> 00:24:50,760
Yes, Mother.

452
00:24:50,990 --> 00:24:53,330
You never had much
of an education either.

453
00:24:57,070 --> 00:25:00,200
Yet you grew the company well.

454
00:25:00,540 --> 00:25:04,440
You are running it well enough,
so far.

455
00:25:04,540 --> 00:25:07,040
Well, Mother...

456
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:14,050
That is all thanks to your guidance
and your leadership.

457
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:15,420
Still, Se Na...

458
00:25:17,420 --> 00:25:20,990
Mother, not getting an education
was my biggest regret.

459
00:25:21,490 --> 00:25:22,760
So while she is young,

460
00:25:22,830 --> 00:25:24,660
I really want her to learn
as much as she can.

461
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:31,670
Since Mom is asking like this,
Grandma,

462
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,870
please let Se Na prepare
to study abroad.

463
00:25:33,940 --> 00:25:35,310
Why are you doing this too, Do Yun?

464
00:25:35,410 --> 00:25:36,840
I am the one saying
I do not want to study.

465
00:25:37,440 --> 00:25:40,380
Grandma, I am never going abroad.

466
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:42,080
I'll recover every cent
of the principal from that debtor...

467
00:25:42,150 --> 00:25:44,680
no matter what. Please give me time.

468
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:49,020
Hey, Se Na. Sweetheart.

469
00:25:49,250 --> 00:25:51,590
She got up before the elders.
How rude of her.

470
00:25:53,090 --> 00:25:54,360
I am sorry, Mother.

471
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:56,530
It is fine.

472
00:25:56,860 --> 00:25:58,900
She must really hate the idea
to do that.

473
00:25:59,460 --> 00:26:02,230
She certainly has a temper.

474
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:08,810
What? Are you sure it is Kim Pro?

475
00:26:09,770 --> 00:26:11,310
Where in Gangwon Province
is he, exactly?

476
00:26:13,210 --> 00:26:14,980
Okay, got it. Thanks.

477
00:26:16,310 --> 00:26:17,310
Darn it.

478
00:26:21,320 --> 00:26:23,750
Wait. Darn it.

479
00:26:28,360 --> 00:26:31,030
What? It is past closing time.

480
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:33,560
Where did everyone go? Mom.

481
00:26:34,230 --> 00:26:35,330
Grandma.

482
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:38,200
Oh, Kkangda, you are here?

483
00:26:38,570 --> 00:26:42,110
Where are you going this late?
Where is everyone? Where is Su Ah?

484
00:26:42,870 --> 00:26:44,870
I don't know. I'm busy.

485
00:26:50,050 --> 00:26:51,050
(Mom)

486
00:26:53,820 --> 00:26:55,150
Where did they go?

487
00:26:58,820 --> 00:27:01,620
- Auntie.
- Oh, Su Ah.

488
00:27:01,830 --> 00:27:03,360
Why are you crying?

489
00:27:04,730 --> 00:27:07,400
- Where did Dad go?
- Auntie...

490
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:09,000
It's alright.

491
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:10,600
Don't cry.

492
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:12,770
Why would you cry?

493
00:27:14,940 --> 00:27:15,940
(Kang Da Mi, My Youngest)

494
00:27:37,260 --> 00:27:39,230
(Kang Da Mi, My Youngest)

495
00:27:59,820 --> 00:28:01,790
(Mission: Mompossible)

496
00:28:01,850 --> 00:28:03,620
It is such a relief our Seung Yun...

497
00:28:04,650 --> 00:28:07,390
- takes after his father, Jun Sung.
- Mother, you know how hard...

498
00:28:07,690 --> 00:28:10,430
- Jin Hee tried.
- About her past...

499
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:11,690
How did she live?

500
00:28:12,030 --> 00:28:14,330
- I am sorry, sweetheart.
- You need to live your life...

501
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:15,770
doing what you enjoy, too.

502
00:28:15,900 --> 00:28:19,140
If you keep living just for us,
you will get sick, Mom.

503
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:22,440
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
